  "explanation": [
    "run2's explicit LD_LIBRARY_PATH is derived from the sorted historical runtime table, placing the gfortran cb4 directory first. This first directory contains all three substituted SONAMEs, so its aliases win over later chqq/xc0 entries.",
    "The fresh diagnostic has DT_RUNPATH (no DT_RPATH); its first compiler support directory is also cb4. The loader trace actually resolved cb4 libquadmath/libstdc++ and cb4's libgcc_s symlink to wy205. This is the observed environment, not merely an inferred future resolution.",
    "A link map records link-time input selection, not the eventual runtime SONAME lookup. Here it selected xc0 libgcc_s and xc0 libquadmath plus cb4 libgfortran. The existing source2 guard expected the historical donor table instead and correctly rejected three path mismatches before any worker started.",
    "The original donor has a direct DT_NEEDED libstdc++.so.6 entry, whereas the fresh diagnostic lacks that direct entry; libstdc++ remains required transitively by libninja. libquadmath remains a transitive libgfortran dependency. All15 actual SONAME providers and every versioned import are present.",
    "A new successor can bind the observed exact 15 resolved paths/hashes while preserving the existing target environment and strict future runtime map checks. These libraries are not byteidentical: this permits only a clearly separated diagnostic run, not an inference of numerical equivalence with the historical campaign."
  ],
